From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: georgewhewell <georgerw@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 18 May 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: xdomain: pin protocol handler owner while
 dispatching

XDomain protocol handlers are called from Thunderbolt control-ring work.
Out-of-tree service modules can unregister and unload while packets are
still being dispatched, because the protocol handler API does not hold a
module reference around the callback.

That leaves a race where tb_xdomain_handle_request() can call stale
module text or data after a reload/unload cycle. Add an optional owner
field to struct tb_protocol_handler and take a temporary module reference
while dispatching. In-flight handlers then make rmmod fail cleanly instead
of letting module memory disappear underneath the callback.

Like ->callback_xd, ->owner lies past the end of the stock struct, so it
is appended last and only read for registrants that left ->callback NULL
(which therefore provide the extended struct).

Signed-off-by: georgewhewell <georgerw@gmail.com>
---

diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/xdomain.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/xdomain.c
index d20b14e..d368042 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/xdomain.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/xdomain.c
@@ -2446,6 +2446,15 @@ bool tb_xdomain_handle_request(struct tb *tb, enum tb_cfg_pkg_type type,
 			continue;
 
 		matched = true;
+		/*
+		 * ->owner (like ->callback_xd) lies past the stock struct;
+		 * only a registrant that left ->callback NULL is known to
+		 * provide it.
+		 */
+		if (!handler->callback && handler->owner &&
+		    !try_module_get(handler->owner))
+			continue;
+
 		mutex_unlock(&xdomain_lock);
 		/*
 		 * ->callback first: a registrant that set it may be built
@@ -2461,6 +2470,9 @@ bool tb_xdomain_handle_request(struct tb *tb, enum tb_cfg_pkg_type type,
 						   handler->data);
 		mutex_lock(&xdomain_lock);
 
+		if (!handler->callback && handler->owner)
+			module_put(handler->owner);
+
 		if (ret)
 			break;
 	}
diff --git a/include/linux/thunderbolt.h b/include/linux/thunderbolt.h
index 7aeae29..2696f2d 100644
--- a/include/linux/thunderbolt.h
+++ b/include/linux/thunderbolt.h
@@ -368,6 +368,9 @@ int tb_xdomain_request(struct tb_xdomain *xd, const void *request,
  *	Appended after @list so every stock member keeps its stock offset:
  *	a registrant built against an unpatched header still interoperates,
  *	and the core reads @callback_xd only when @callback is NULL.
+ * @owner: Optional module that owns @callback_xd. If set, XDomain core
+ *	pins it while dispatching to avoid unload races. Appended after
+ *	@callback_xd and read under the same @callback-is-NULL rule.
  *
  * Thunderbolt services can hook into incoming XDomain requests by
  * registering protocol handler. Only limitation is that the XDomain
@@ -378,6 +381,8 @@ int tb_xdomain_request(struct tb_xdomain *xd, const void *request,
  * directed to the service the driver implements.
  */
 #define TB_PROTOCOL_HANDLER_HAS_XDOMAIN 1
+#define TB_PROTOCOL_HANDLER_HAS_OWNER 1
+struct module;
 struct tb_protocol_handler {
 	const uuid_t *uuid;
 	int (*callback)(const void *buf, size_t size, void *data);
@@ -385,6 +390,7 @@ struct tb_protocol_handler {
 	struct list_head list;
 	int (*callback_xd)(struct tb_xdomain *xd, const void *buf, size_t size,
 			   void *data);
+	struct module *owner;
 };
 
 int tb_register_protocol_handler(struct tb_protocol_handler *handler);
-- 
